{"author":{"id":"1d21e70a32f794e19f8d3626c963a95c52102f79bd1dc44e2b4b611903f1b863"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1780991930,"nonce":"/qrbc8E6q1A3Gm71lfQo2qjZx9o=","target":"8f34a1755261651f041cd898ed1ffc3882ca5bd31fc2a647dbede6ba6278c8a4","message":"The Perfect Commit\n==================\n\nIdeally each commit should package implementation, tests, documentation, and a link to the issue.\n\nTests\n-----\n\nThis feels kind of difficult for Nix config - we can configure NixOS VM tests at most.\n\nDocumentation\n-------------\n\nThe repo should definitely include a `docs/` or `wiki/` directory that is updated alongside the implementations as a reference and guide for what was added.\nNote that this should be human-written as much as possible primarily to avoid overly verbose documentation.\n\n\nIssues\n------\n`git-bug` works great, however I was unable to push to the git remote due to \n\n- https://simonwillison.net/2022/Oct/29/the-perfect-commit","files":null},{"type":6,"timestamp":1780992045,"nonce":"KBiVnnB0U/ZABa0G4EA2uqvas4Y=","target":"8f34a1755261651f041cd898ed1ffc3882ca5bd31fc2a647dbede6ba6278c8a4","message":"The Perfect Commit\n==================\n\nIdeally each commit should package implementation, tests, documentation, and a link to the issue.\n\nTests\n-----\n\nThis feels kind of difficult for Nix config - we can configure NixOS VM tests at most.\n\nDocumentation\n-------------\n\nThe repo should definitely include a `docs/` or `wiki/` directory that is updated alongside the implementations as a reference and guide for what was added.\nNote that this should be human-written as much as possible primarily to avoid overly verbose documentation.\n\n\nIssues\n------\n`git-bug` works great, however I was unable to push to the git remote due to this error: \n\n```sh\nError: ssh: handshake failed: ssh: unable to authenticate, attempted methods [none publickey], no supported methods remain\n```\n\nThe cause of this issue (investigated by Claudius) is that the SSH library that `git-bug` uses only supports authentication with the ssh-agent, not falling back to the SSH key.\nThusly, I implemented user services to run `ssh-add ~/.ssh/id_ed25519` on login.\n\n\nReferences\n----------\n\n- https://simonwillison.net/2022/Oct/29/the-perfect-commit","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1780992070,"nonce":"EtzcDH9jjfGNK7ZAcBUyzBQ5xQo=","message":"git-bug is not very ergonomic except in the tui - should add an alias for the tui before merging","files":null}]}